# Folkprotocol Verification v0
#
# Seventh experimental slice. Three independent read-only audits check the tone
# draft. They write reports and never silently repair or publish it.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

Parallel(3):
    Codex: """Audit citation completeness and provenance in
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md against 00-commission.md, the six
source maps from 10 through 60, 70-practice-strains.md,
80-practice-assessment.md, 90-protocol-dossiers.md, and
100-factual-draft.md.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 10-reddit-forums.md 20-traditional.md
30-published-research.md 40-commercial-web.md 50-experimental-communities.md
60-practitioner-folk-web.md 70-practice-strains.md 80-practice-assessment.md
90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md 120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`.
Write it as inputDigest in the YAML frontmatter of
research/source-maps/{slug}/130-citation-audit.md. If that file ends with
`CITATION AUDIT COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it unchanged. Do no
web research and do not edit any existing file. Write only 130-citation-audit.md.
Work yourself: do not delegate, spawn subagents, or start another agent workflow.
Check every citation token in
the prose, every reference entry, exact source-ID existence, reference
expansion, numerical claims, preparation/timing claims, and whether the cited
source actually supports the adjacent wording. Check that all factual-draft
citations and material qualifications survived the tone rewrite. Report only
concrete mismatches with exact phrases and source locations. If none, write
`CLEAN`. End with `CITATION AUDIT COMPLETE`.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1800

    Codex: """Audit the substantive shape of
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md against 00-commission.md,
70-practice-strains.md, 80-practice-assessment.md, 90-protocol-dossiers.md, and
100-factual-draft.md.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 70-practice-strains.md 80-practice-assessment.md
90-protocol-dossiers.md 100-factual-draft.md 120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`.
Write it as inputDigest in the YAML frontmatter of
research/source-maps/{slug}/131-content-audit.md. If that file ends with
`CONTENT AUDIT COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it unchanged. Do no
web research and do not edit existing files. Write only 131-content-audit.md.
Work yourself: do not delegate, spawn subagents, or start another agent workflow.
Look for concrete failures:
lost source traditions, a laundry list replacing the selected architecture,
one evidence type silently used as a universal hierarchy, speculative material
laundered into fact or deleted, protocol details invented beyond the dossiers,
symptom relief confused with prevention or clearance, or generic safety copy
that displaces useful content. Do not demand RCTs or propose a different page
merely from preference. If none, write `CLEAN`. End with
`CONTENT AUDIT COMPLETE`.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1800

    CC: """Audit the prose of
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md against 110-tone-brief.md. Do not
read 121-tone-review.md, 130-citation-audit.md, or 131-content-audit.md: this
must be an independent read, not a repetition of earlier findings. Solely for
the idempotency check below, you may inspect the existing 132-tone-audit.md
frontmatter inputDigest and final marker; do not read or reuse its findings.
Do not read other project pages, search the web, or edit the draft. From
research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input
digest with exactly
`sha256sum 110-tone-brief.md 120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`.
Write it as inputDigest in the YAML frontmatter of
research/source-maps/{slug}/132-tone-audit.md. If that file ends with
`FINAL TONE AUDIT COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it unchanged.
Write only 132-tone-audit.md. Work yourself: do not delegate, spawn subagents,
or start another agent workflow.

Report concrete remaining instances of medical-site voice, evidence-status
tics, assistant cadence, canned warmth, repeated mini-verdicts, qualifications
that bury the observation, or laundry-list prose. Do not object merely because
the page makes a judgment, uses first or second person, or includes thin and
strange material. Do not suggest removing a useful effect size, exact community
amount, source-access boundary, population limit, or material qualification.
Do not turn a failed search into proof of absence, add an intervention claim to
replace evidence-status wording, or exchange an observational result for a
causal claim. Source-kind language is appropriate where it tells the reader
what kind of record an amount or claim comes from. Give exact phrases and local
repairs. If none, write `CLEAN`. End with `FINAL TONE AUDIT COMPLETE`.""" model=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1200
